[05:52.00] where she laid the egg,
[05:53.00] what time of day she laid the egg,
[05:55.00] bring the egg in,
[05:57.00] assort the egg, lay the egg up,
[05:59.00] tell the lady about the egg,
[06:03.00] and go shore the hen.
[06:04.00] And then she'd go out and pet the hen
[06:06.00] and then when night come
[06:08.00] I'd have to go get the hen again
[06:09.00] and set her back up on the ice box
[06:11.00] to where she could be safe from all harm
[06:14.00] and I used to carry her hay,
[06:15.00] 14 blocks across town from a leverage table
[06:18.00] and a tow sack I'd have to make
